# Test Plan: Program List Filtering and Display

**Feature:** Program list filtering and display  
**Actor:** Admin user  
**Primary UI:** **Programs** page — program **list** showing **Name** and **Description** (and any additional columns the product adds)  
**Sample programs (concrete data):**

| Name | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Web Development 2026 | Cohort covering HTML, CSS, and JavaScript fundamentals. |
| Informatique & IA - Niveau 2 | Programme avancé en intelligence artificielle et systèmes. |
| Test Program | Short-lived program used for QA scenarios. |

**Note:** The stakeholder **Description** in the source story mentions duplicate name prevention; that does not match the **Task** or **Acceptance Criteria** (list display and empty state). This plan covers **list display**, **empty state**, and **filtering** where the product provides it (task title includes “filtering”; ACs do not—see **Ambiguities**).

---

## Positive flows

### TC-001
- **Title:** Programs page lists every program’s **Name** and **Description**  
- **Preconditions:** Logged in as admin; at least three programs exist: **Web Development 2026**, **Informatique & IA - Niveau 2**, and **Test Program**, with the **Description** values from the table above.  
- **Steps:**
  1. Navigate to the **Programs** page (via main nav or deep link per product).
  2. For each seeded program, locate its row or card in the list.
  3. Verify visible text for **Name** and **Description** matches the stored values (allowing for documented truncation with “show more” if applicable).
- **Expected result:** The list shows all existing programs; each item displays **Name** and **Description** (or full **Description** via expand control if that is the design); no program is missing from the default unfiltered view.  
- **Priority:** High  
- **Maps to AC:** Display program list with key details  

---

### TC-002
- **Title:** Empty state shows clear message and prompt to create the first program  
- **Preconditions:** No programs exist in the environment (fresh tenant, data reset, or delete-all in non-production); admin user.  
- **Steps:**
  1. Navigate to the **Programs** page.
  2. Read the empty-state **message** and any **call-to-action** (e.g. button or link).
- **Expected result:** User sees messaging that **no programs have been created** (or equivalent plain-language copy); user sees an explicit **prompt to create the first program** (e.g. **Create program**, **Add program**, or link to creation flow); list area is not a blank white gap with no explanation.  
- **Priority:** High  
- **Maps to AC:** Empty state when no programs exist  

---

### TC-003
- **Title:** Create-first-program prompt routes to program creation with working form  
- **Preconditions:** Same as TC-002 (no programs).  
- **Steps:**
  1. From empty state, activate the **create first program** control.
  2. Confirm the **program creation** form opens (or correct step in wizard).
- **Expected result:** Navigation succeeds; user can enter **Name** and **Description** and complete create per existing create-story tests.  
- **Priority:** Medium  

---

### TC-004
- **Title:** After creating the first program from empty state, list replaces empty state with row showing **Name** and **Description**  
- **Preconditions:** Empty state (TC-002); user initiates create from prompt.  
- **Steps:**
  1. Create program **Name** `Data Literacy 2026`, **Description** `Foundations of data analysis for business users.`
  2. Submit; land on or return to **Programs** page.
- **Expected result:** Empty state is gone; list shows **Data Literacy 2026** with matching **Description**.  
- **Priority:** High  

---

### TC-005
- **Title:** Filter or search by program **Name** narrows the list (when filter UI exists)  
- **Preconditions:** Programs **Web Development 2026**, **Informatique & IA - Niveau 2**, **Test Program** exist; **Programs** page includes a **search** box, **Name** filter, or equivalent. *If no filter UI ships, mark this case **N/A** and track as product gap vs task title.*  
- **Steps:**
  1. Open **Programs** page.
  2. Enter filter text `Web Development` (or apply filter matching that substring).
  3. Observe rows.
- **Expected result:** Only programs whose **Name** matches the filter rule appear (at minimum **Web Development 2026**); other names hidden until filter cleared.  
- **Priority:** Medium  

---

### TC-006
- **Title:** Clearing filters restores full program list  
- **Preconditions:** Same as TC-005; filter applied so fewer than all programs show.  
- **Steps:**
  1. Clear search text or reset filter control.
- **Expected result:** All programs from TC-001 set visible again (subject to pagination rules).  
- **Priority:** Medium  

